        "original_id": "9f479b68-84e8-5893-be42-85f8e3fe5e1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Graham Hill, Richie Ginther, Bruce McLaren\n- Events: 1962 Italian Grand Prix, 1963 Lombank Trophy\n- Roles: racing driver, team owner, Formula One World Champion\n- Products: BRM P57, Cooper\n\nFacts:\n- At the 1962 Italian Grand Prix, Graham Hill's teammate Richie Ginther finished second and Cooper driver Bruce McLaren finished third.\n- Norman Graham Hill was born on 15 February 1929 and died on 29 November 1975.\n- Graham Hill was a British racing driver and team owner from England.\n- Graham Hill was twice Formula One World Champion.\n- The 1963 Lombank Trophy was run over 50 laps of the circuit.\n- British driver Graham Hill won the 1963 Lombank Trophy in a BRM P57.",
